{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c7d753ff-ee70-49e5-a4c5-ee5484c6d1e7",
    "name": "RGBoo API",
    "description": "The RGBoo cloud API (cloud_api/), which accepts colour requests, paces them one per 20 seconds, and parks them in Firestore for the home-machine bridge to dispatch.\n\nPick an environment first: **RGBoo Local** or **RGBoo Cloud Run**.\n\nEvery request sends `X-Api-Key: {{api_key}}` from the collection auth, except `GET /` (open by design, for uptime checks) and the two requests in **Auth** that deliberately send a bad key.\n\nNote: requests created here are real. They sit in the queue until the bridge dispatches them or you run **Clear queue**.\n\nThe **Admin** folder needs `admin_key` as well, a separate and more privileged secret than `api_key`.\n\nSee docs/architecture.md and docs/admin-clear-current.md.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "apikey",
    "apikey": [
      {
        "key": "key",
        "value": "X-Api-Key",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "value",
        "value": "{{api_key}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "in",
        "value": "header",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Fail fast with a clear message instead of a confusing 401/ECONNREFUSED.",
          "if (!pm.environment.get('base_url')) {",
          "  throw new Error('No base_url set \u2014 select the RGBoo Local or RGBoo Cloud Run environment.');",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ""
              ]
            },
            "description": "Open endpoint \u2014 no API key required, so uptime checks need no secret. Reports whether Firestore is reachable and whether the bridge has sent a heartbeat in the last 2 minutes.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('reports healthy', () => pm.expect(b.status).to.eql('healthy'));",
                  "pm.test('reports bridge liveness', () => pm.expect(b).to.have.property('bridge_online'));",
                  "// serial_connected is null when the bridge is offline, false in --dry-run.",
                  "console.log('bridge_online:', b.bridge_online, '| serial_connected:', b.serial_connected);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Colour",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Submit a colour",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/color",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "color"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The main endpoint. Validates, assigns the next 20-second slot, and writes a pending document. Saves request_id and scheduled_time to environment variables for the requests that follow.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"postman\",\n  \"color\": {\n    \"r\": 255,\n    \"g\": 0,\n    \"b\": 0\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('queued', () => pm.expect(b.status).to.eql('queued'));",
                  "pm.test('returns the contract fields', () => {",
                  "  ['request_id','queue_position','estimated_wait_seconds','scheduled_time'].forEach(",
                  "    k => pm.expect(b).to.have.property(k));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('echoes the colour back', () => pm.expect(b.color).to.eql({r:255,g:0,b:0}));",
                  "pm.environment.set('last_request_id', b.request_id);",
                  "pm.environment.set('last_scheduled_time', b.scheduled_time);",
                  "console.log('scheduled for', b.scheduled_time, '- in', b.estimated_wait_seconds, 'seconds');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Submit a second colour (pacing)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/color",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "color"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Run straight after the previous request. Its slot must be exactly 20 seconds later \u2014 that spacing is enforced by a Firestore transaction, so it holds even with concurrent requests hitting different API instances.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"postman-two\",\n  \"color\": {\n    \"r\": 0,\n    \"g\": 0,\n    \"b\": 255\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "const prev = pm.environment.get('last_scheduled_time');",
                  "pm.test('slot is 20s after the previous one', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(prev, 'run \"Submit a colour\" first').to.be.a('string');",
                  "  const gap = (new Date(b.scheduled_time) - new Date(prev)) / 1000;",
                  "  pm.expect(gap).to.eql(20);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.environment.set('last_scheduled_time', b.scheduled_time);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
